Version 2.0 of "top", the top processes display for Berkeley Unix, has
been posted to "mod.sources" and should be appearing in about a week.  For
those of you with ARPANet access, it is already available via anonymous
FTP from host "dione.rice.edu".  Log in as "anonymous" with any password
and retrieve the file "public/top.shar" (about 87K bytes), then run it
through your favorite shell.

This version will work on standard 4.2 systems as well as Sun UNIX
(version 2 or 3) and Pyramid Unix.  Sorry it took so long.

